# GGO panel crates

* Do not call `TilesetDocStore::state()` to read one field: it clones the
  whole pixel buffer (~64KB). Use the borrowing accessors -- `indices()`,
  `palette()`, `tile_count()`, `dirty()` -- and reserve `state()` for
  callers that genuinely need an owned snapshot (tests, save). Seventeen
  production call sites had this wrong at once, and an eighteenth slipped
  past the sweep that fixed them.

* A preview must CONSUME the commit's producer, never mirror it. Two
  shipped branches lied to the user this way: the shape preview drew
  `shape_points(false)` while release painted `shape_points(shift)`, and
  the float preview duplicated `commit_float`'s compositing until both were
  routed through one `float_cells`. If you are about to write a "keep these
  in lockstep" comment, extract the shared producer instead.

* Panels expose smoke-test hooks through a `test-support` cargo feature as
  `test_*` methods -- never by widening `pub(crate)` internals. The
  established pattern lives in `ggo_tileset_panel`, `ggo_import_panel` and
  `ggo_emerald_panel`; `ggo_smoke` is the consumer. Whole-journey tests
  belong in `ggo_smoke`, per-feature regressions in the panel's own crate.

* `cargo fmt -p <crate>` is safe here NOW, but was not always: audio_panel
  and emu_panel carried ~570 lines of drift until 2026-08-28's dedicated
  formatting commit, and the ggo repo's worldlib still drifts (its own
  `.rules` says so). Before running a package-wide fmt in any ggo crate,
  `cargo fmt -p <crate> --check` first; if untouched files appear, format
  in a dedicated commit, never inside a feature diff.
